@title Runbook: manual failover of orders-aurora-prod
@subtitle Database Reliability · Fenwick Bank

# When to use this runbook

Use it when the writer instance has been unhealthy for more than 5 minutes and automatic failover has not happened. Also use it for a planned failover during the Sunday maintenance window (02:00 to 04:00 UTC).

# Prerequisites

- The break-glass role db-failover-operator
- Access to the #db-incidents channel
- The replica lag dashboard, open

# Failover steps

1. Announce the failover in #db-incidents.
2. Confirm replica lag on the target reader is under 30 seconds.
3. Put the orders service into read-only mode with the feature flag orders.readonly.

!! **Never fail over to a reader whose lag exceeds 30 seconds.** Committed orders will be lost.

4. Trigger the failover to reader instance orders-aurora-prod-r2.
5. Wait for the cluster endpoint to point at the new writer (usually 30 to 60 seconds).
6. Turn orders.readonly off.
7. Watch the connection count recover to its normal level of about 400.

# Verification

table = Check,Expected; Writer instance,orders-aurora-prod-r2; Replica lag,under 1 second; Error rate on orders API,under 0.5%; Connections,about 400

# Rollback

If the new writer is unhealthy, fail back to orders-aurora-prod-r1 using the same steps, and escalate to the on-call DBA lead.
